// A reusable button, meant to be included and then completed by whoever uses it.
//
// Included from Rust with `bsn! { :"scenes/dynamic_bsn_button.bsn" }`, and from another `.bsn`
// file with `:"scenes/dynamic_bsn_button.bsn"`. Include paths are relative to the asset root,
// never to the file that names them, and the include must be the first thing in an entity —
// before its `#Name`, its components and its relations.
//
// Type paths may be written in full (`bevy_ui::ui_node::Node`) or, when the short name is
// unambiguous in the type registry, short (`Node`). This file uses the short form.
//
// Note the deliberate absence of a `Children` block: children coming from a base and children
// coming from the file that includes it are *appended*, not merged pairwise, so a label written
// here would end up next to the includer's label rather than being replaced by it. A base that
// expects to be completed leaves the slot empty.
Node {
    width: Val::Px(180.0),
    height: Val::Px(56.0),
    justify_content: JustifyContent::Center,
    align_items: AlignItems::Center,
}
// `.bsn` has no access to Rust items, so there are no constants (`Color::WHITE`) and no
// constructor calls (`Color::srgb(...)`): colors are written out as struct literals.
BackgroundColor(Color::Srgba(Srgba {
    red: 0.15,
    green: 0.15,
    blue: 0.15,
    alpha: 1.0,
}))
